				11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				14.55
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Peripl.M.Rubr.</u>
				60
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν Ἰταλίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					13.3
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν Κρήτην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Act.Ap.</u>
					27.8
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				13
			</span></i> : abs., <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				13.1.22
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>speak beside</i> the purpose, <i>wander in one's talk,
			rave</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολλὰ π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Epid.</u>
				1.18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				26
			</span></i>.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ᾽</span> :—
				Med.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραλεξάμενος</span>
			<i>speaking beside the point</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1.101
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>speak incidentally</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῦθον</span>”
